# AWS Cognito + IoT Core Configuration
# This file is for reference only - configuration is done in the browser dashboard

# AWS Region
AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# AWS Cognito Identity Pool ID
# Get this from: AWS Console -> Cognito -> Manage Identity Pools -> Dashboard
# Format: us-east-1:xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx
COGNITO_IDENTITY_POOL_ID=us-east-1:your-identity-pool-id-here

# AWS IoT Core Endpoint
# Get this from: AWS Console -> IoT Core -> Settings -> Custom endpoint
# Format: xxxxx-ats.iot.region.amazonaws.com
AWS_IOT_ENDPOINT=a2jxq81rsqt8vu-ats.iot.us-east-1.amazonaws.com

# MQTT Topic to subscribe to
# This should match the topic your ESP32 publishes to
AWS_IOT_TOPIC=sws-data

# ============================================
# Notes:
# ============================================

# 1. Browser Configuration:
#    - Open dashboard-cognito.html in your browser
#    - Click "AWS Configuration" button
#    - Enter the values above
#    - Click "Connect"

# 2. No Backend Server Required:
#    - The new Cognito-based approach doesn't need server.js
#    - The HTML file connects directly to AWS IoT Core
#    - Credentials are temporary and fetched from Cognito

# 3. Security:
#    - Never commit actual Identity Pool IDs to version control
#    - Use IAM policies to restrict access (see COGNITO_SETUP.md)
#    - Configure proper CORS if hosting on a domain

# 4. Setup Guide:
#    - See COGNITO_SETUP.md for complete setup instructions
#    - Follow the step-by-step guide to configure Cognito and IAM

# ============================================
# Legacy Configuration (for server.js)
# ============================================
# If you still want to use the server.js proxy approach,
# use the env.example file instead
